_mediatisation","c":2},{"y":1801,"t":"loss","x":"9 February 1801: the left bank goes to France.","m":2,"cp":"french-consulate","cpn":"French Consulate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","c":2},{"y":1803,"t":"loss","x":"1803: the Duchy of Westphalia goes to Hesse-Darmstadt.","cp":"landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt","cpn":"Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Cologne","c":3},{"y":1803,"t":"dissolve","x":"February 1803: the Reichsdeputationshauptschluss secularizes the electorate.","m":2,"cp":"landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt","cpn":"Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Cologne","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"War of the Limburg Succession","from":1288,"to":1289,"outcome":"Brabant wins at Worringen (5 June 1288); Cologne becomes independent of the archbishop; Limburg is added to Brabant in 1289.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Worringen"},{"name":"Soest Feud","from":1444,"to":1449,"outcome":"Soest accepts Cleves-Mark as suzerain and is lost to Cologne.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soest_Feud"},{"name":"Cologne War","from":1583,"to":1588,"outcome":"Ernst of Bavaria wins; the Wittelsbachs hold the archbishopric to 1761.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cologne_War"},{"name":"French Revolutionary Wars (Electorate of Cologne)","from":1794,"to":1801,"outcome":"France occupies Cologne and Bonn in 1794 and takes the left bank in 1801 (Lunéville).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Cologne"}],"certainty":[{"from":953,"to":1803,"level":"soft","note":"The pages give no boundaries; the lands lay in scattered blocks (Rhine, Westphalia)."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Cologne","title":"Electorate of Cologne"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Westphalia","title":"Duchy of Westphalia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Worringen","title":"Battle of Worringen"},{"url":"https://en.wik